# Testing — yes-toto

## Scope

The Makefile `test` target builds and runs **`build/tests/test_core`** (or `build/tests/test_core.exe` on Windows).

Tests cover **`fill_buffer()`** only. There are **no** subprocess/integration tests in-tree; the infinite output loop is not unit-tested.

## Layout

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `tests/test_runner.c` | `main()` — invokes all suites in fixed order |
| `tests/test_fill_one_byte.c` / `.h` | 1-byte line fills buffer completely |
| `tests/test_fill_divides_exact.c` / `.h` | `line_len` divides `buf_size` evenly |
| `tests/test_fill_indivisible.c` / `.h` | slack at end not written; return is multiple of `line_len` |
| `tests/test_fill_line_eq_buf.c` / `.h` | `line_len == buf_size` → exactly one copy |
| `tests/test_fill_ub_note.c` / `.h` | documents `line_len > buf_size` as precondition violation (UB); not exercised |

One scenario per `.c` / `.h` pair; headers declare the test function for `test_runner.c`.

## Framework

- No external framework — plain C with `<assert.h>`.
- Each case prints `PASS: <descriptive name>` on success.
- `assert()` failure → `abort()` → non-zero exit from `make test`.

## Build (from `Makefile`)

Objects and the test binary live under `build/tests/`:

```makefile
TEST_CORE := build/tests/test_core
# $(TEST_BUILD_DIR)/%.o ← tests/%.c
# link $(TEST_CORE) from $(TEST_OBJS)
test: $(TEST_CORE)
	./$(TEST_CORE)
```

`fill_buffer()` comes from `#include "yes_toto.h"` in each test file — **no link with `src/*.c`**.

## Required cases (behaviour)

1. One-byte line: returned length `== buf_size`.
2. Divisible: returned length `== buf_size`, multiple of `line_len`.
3. Indivisible: e.g. buf 10, line `"abc"` → return 9; multiple of `line_len`.
4. `line_len == buf_size`: one full `memcpy`.
5. `line_len > buf_size`: **undefined** per API contract — print PASS note only; do not call `fill_buffer()`.

## Adding tests

- Add `tests/test_fill_<name>.c` + `.h`, declare runner function in `.h`, call from `test_runner.c`, append to `TEST_SRCS` in `Makefile`.
- Keep tests allocation-free; stack buffers only.

## Manual smoke tests (not automated)

After `make`:

```sh
./build/yes-toto --version
./build/yes-toto --help
./build/yes-toto | head -n 3    # expect exit 0, no stderr (pipe / 64 KiB path)
./build/yes-toto hello | head -n 1
# Interactive: ./build/yes-toto then Ctrl+C — expect exit 130; terminal stays responsive
```
